  "summary_en": "Hong Kong's Small Unmanned Aircraft Order (L.N. 116 of 2021, effective 1 June 2022) regulates drones up to 25 kg. It classifies them by weight, and requires aircraft and remote pilot registration, insurance, a safety system with flight data recording, and permissions for restricted zones. It also sets offences and enforcement powers.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Drones up to 25 kg are classified as A1 (≤250 g), A2 (≤7 kg) or B (>7 kg).",
   "Aircraft and remote pilots must be registered; pilots need ratings, and category B flights need permission.",
   "Third-party liability insurance of HK$5–10 million is required for non-enclosed flights.",
   "Aircraft need a safety system recording location, altitude and speed, with data kept for 6 months.",
   "Offences for dangerous operation, flying in restricted zones and carrying dangerous goods carry a level 6 fine and 2 years' imprisonment."
  ],
